<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     MÓDULO JS: CLIMA PALEOCLIMÁTICO — PaleoBot
     ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     FUENTES CIENTÍFICAS ACTUALIZADAS (2020-2025):

     δ¹⁸O / VOLUMEN DE HIELO GLOBAL:
       · Westerhold et al. (2020). An astronomically dated record of Earth's
         climate and its predictability over the last 66 million years.
         Science 369(6509):1383-1387. DOI: 10.1126/science.aba6853
         [Cenozoic stack CENOGRID — resolución orbital, 0-66 Ma]

       · Lear et al. (2016). Deep Atlantic Ocean carbon storage and the rise
         of 100,000-year glacial cycles.
         Nature Geoscience 9:630-634. DOI: 10.1038/ngeo2757
         [Stack Î´¹³C bentónico — MPT 0.9-1.2 Ma]

     TEMPERATURA GLOBAL — ERA COMÚN:
       · PAGES 2k Consortium (2019). Consistent multidecadal variability in
         global temperature reconstructions and simulations over the Common Era.
         Nature Geoscience 12:643-649. DOI: 10.1038/s41561-019-0400-0
         [692 proxies · 7 regiones · CE 1-2000]

       · Neukom et al. (2019). No evidence for globally coherent warm and cold
         periods over the preindustrial Common Era.
         Nature 571:550-554. DOI: 10.1038/s41586-019-1401-2
         [Análisis PAGESHydro2k]

     TEMPERATURA CUATERNARIA (HIELO ANTÁRTICO):
       · Extier et al. (2018, actualizado 2022 en NOAA NCEI).
         EPICA Dome C 800 Ka composite temperature record.
         NOAA World Data Service for Paleoclimatology.
         https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/access/paleo-search/study/17839

     ESTADIOS ISOTÓPICOS MARINOS:
       · Railsback et al. (2015, referencia estándar en uso 2020-2025).
         An optimized scheme of lettered marine isotope substages for the
         last 1.0 million years, and the climatostratigraphic nature of
         isotope stages and substages. Quaternary Science Reviews 111:94-106.
         DOI: 10.1016/j.quascirev.2015.01.012

       · Cohen, K.M., Finney, S.C., Gibbard, P.L. & Fan, J.-X. (2013; updated).
         The ICS International Chronostratigraphic Chart (v2023/09).
         Episodes 36(3):199-204. Cita recomendada por la ICS; corrige la
         referencia «Cohen et al. 2023, Episodes 46(2)», no localizada (PB-GH-03).

     EVENTOS HEINRICH Y D-O:
       · Menviel et al. (2020). An ice-climate oscillatory framework for
         Dansgaard-Oeschger cycles. Nature Reviews Earth & Environment 1:677-693.
         DOI: 10.1038/s43017-020-00106-y

       · Rasmussen et al. (2014, base estándar NGRIP actualizada 2022).
         A stratigraphic framework for abrupt climatic changes during the
         Last Glacial period based on three synchronized Greenland ice-core
         records. Quaternary Science Reviews 106:14-28.
         DOI: 10.1016/j.quascirev.2014.09.007

     CONTEXTO HOMÍNINO-CLIMÁTICO:
       · Potts et al. (2020). Increased ecological resource variability during
         a critical transition in hominin evolution. Science Advances 6(43).
         DOI: 10.1126/sciadv.abc8975

       · Trauth et al. (2021). Classifying past climate change in the
         Turkana Basin, East Africa, and its relation to early hominin evolution.
         Quaternary Science Reviews 270:107170.
         DOI: 10.1016/j.quascirev.2021.107170

     NOTA: Los arrays numéricos embebidos son puntos representativos
     de los stacks publicados. Para análisis de investigación, usa
     los datasets completos en NOAA NCEI Paleoclimatology:
     https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/products/paleoclimatology
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
